  "implementation_scope": [
    "One original SubmissionSource terminal supports effect-only continuations with no pending tensor input. Source-required registration is retained even when the real COW read list is empty.",
    "ResourceFullRange.readable_bytes bounds full-writer tickets to genuinely written prefixes. Effect admission selects only original ready/full/append permissions covering the actual registered read ranges; an empty read list grants none.",
    "The successor owns fresh targets and retains the predecessor Source metadata owner, not its writer/tail or returned transaction pointer. Final ready inheritance clones real bounded guards from the successfully published predecessor cache."
  ],
  "checked": [
    "COW variant: original three-row snapshot, A appends two rows to five, B copies A partial tail to its distinct page and appends one row to six. Exact BF16 row values, original snapshot and A prefix remain correct.",
    "Page-boundary variant: A appends three rows to six, B adds one row to a new page with no COW effect reads. It still reports one Source/device wait and zero host waits and rejects ordinary submit.",
    "Both variants use actual pending A, one original Queue and a controlled pending B. A retires and detaches; its returned transaction is published while B stays pending. That transaction and local A frame are destroyed before B ready inheritance.",
    "COW source coverage accepts the original 128 bytes and rejects 129 bytes inside the same physical page. A separately malformed effect descriptor is rejected before the unchanged complete bundle binds successfully.",
    "COW A tail reservation is unavailable while its admitted B reader remains active, then succeeds and rolls back after B retirement.",
    "The same final process also passes two nominated-effect boundary checks, ten token/Store/Hybrid Source cases and the retained explicit/private metadata attention cases."
  ],
